1-Longhorn can be installed on Rancher as a Rancher application Or on a separate RKE2 cluster 

2- Longhorn should be installed on the same rke2 cluster that runs the application pods

3- Longhorn Provides distributed block storage for Kubernetes 
====>  Distributed block storage refers to a storage architecture in which data is stored
across multiple physical devices or nodes, and these devices work together to provide a unified and scalable
storage system. (you can have multiple nodes in longhorn and data is spread across those nodes)

4- Prepare Storage: Longhorn requires dedicated storage for its default volume data path, which is
/var/lib/longhorn. Ensure you have a dedicated disk ready and mount it with the appropriate filesystem,
typically ext4 or xfs, to store Longhorn's volume data.

5- Have one or more additional dedicated disks that need to have a supported file system on them.

6-  important feature available is the ability to allocate a minimum amount of CPU to the Instance
manager. This allocation ensures that the Instance manager, responsible for controller and replica instance
lifecycle management, has the necessary computational resources to operate efficiently. By setting a
minimum CPU allocation, you can guarantee that Longhorn's core components receive the required
processing power for optimal performance.

7- V2 can be particularly attractive for:
databases
high-IOPS applications
NVMe
low-latency workloads
large storage systems

V1 is for general use. 

8- Choose V1 if:
You want the simplest deployment.
Your applications have normal I/O requirements.
You're running VMs/general applications/databases without extreme storage performance requirements.
You want maximum maturity.
You want fewer infrastructure prerequisites.
You don't have NVMe-focused hardware.

Consider V2 if:
You're using modern NVMe storage.
You need very high IOPS.
Latency matters significantly.
You have database workloads that can benefit from very fast storage.
You're comfortable managing SPDK/hugepages/hardware prerequisites.
You've tested the exact V2 feature set you need.

9- The Engine Image is the software that actually runs the Longhorn storage engine for a volume.
Think of it as the "storage engine binary/container". Longhorn needs an engine image installed/available on the nodes that will run the engine.

                  Longhorn Volume
                        │
                        ▼
                 Engine Image
